  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">This print run is composed of 28 hand-bound, numbered copies.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Screw post binding in white paper wrapper. Wrapper exterior has quotation printed in black on exterior from pages 21-23 of La poética de la ensoñación by Gastón Bachlard. Inside wrapper has reproductions of two photographs and colophon hand-written by author with number of item. Each page of volume is hand-stamped with a date on the bottom, starting with 16 Mar. 2020 and ending with 28 June 2021. From 16 Mar. to  09 Ago. it seems continuous. After 9 Ago 2020 there is a blank page and the dates pick up again with 27 Mar. 2021 to 28 Apr. 2021, some of which are blue paper. The last pages are from  21 Jun. 2021 to 28 Jun. 2021. Some of the pages in the first section have printed reproductions of photographed attached with paper clips.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"(El cielo está, por encima del techo / tan azul, tan calmo.)(The sky above the roof / Is so blue, so calm!.) is the second part of the trilogy that began with "The poetic reverie, on the contrary...", in which the image of the house is explored from a quotation found in a book by the philosopher Gaston Bachelard. If, in the first part, the search for the house was produced by the visual conformation of its façade - obtained from photographic archives due to the impossibility of obtaining this image due to the quarantine - in this second part, the skies seen from inside the house are the only photographs that make up this book [attached with paperclips]. As a tribute to On Kawara's million years, this publication acts as a hand-stamped calendar of those monotonous days of confinement, whose only variable element was, in many cases, looking out of the window and noticing the clouds, their changing shapes, their colors." -- publisher's website, viewed 06/04/2024.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Title from white paper wrapper.</subfield>
  </datafield>
